# .gitignore — things that must never enter the project's history.
#
# Raw data is NOT ignored, except the bulk GRIB cache (DECISIONS D47, see the
# rule near the end of this file). Raw pulls are committed on purpose (D15),
# because the immutable-snapshot rule (SPEC 2.3) only means something if the
# snapshot is actually in the history.

# --- macOS clutter ---
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# --- Python clutter ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- editor and OS odds and ends ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
Thumbs.db

# --- Claude Code local settings (audit A67-08) ---
.claude/

# --- the large GRIB cache: the one exception to "raw data is committed" ---
# DECISIONS D47: the ~20 GB GFS GRIB cache can be fetched again, so its bytes
# are not committed. Its provenance is committed instead, as the pull
# manifests under data/raw/diagnostics/. No trailing slash, so a cache that is
# a symbolic link is ignored too (audit A68a-06).
data/raw/grib

# --- scratch GRIB files a pull script leaves behind only if killed mid-pull
# (audit A67-08). Matches _scratch_*.grib2 only, never the tracked samples.
data/raw/diagnostics/**/_scratch_*.grib2
